// Zed keymap — additive only.
//
// `base_keymap: "JetBrains"` already provides the verbs that matter, and they
// were checked against Zed 1.14.2's own keymap files rather than assumed:
//
//   cmd-alt-l              editor::Format          (IDEA "Reformat Code")
//   ctrl-alt-r / shift-f10 task::Spawn             (IDEA "Run Anything")
//   cmd-f5                 task::Rerun
//   alt-f12                terminal_panel::Toggle
//   cmd-?                  agent::ToggleFocus
//   cmd-shift-e            project_panel::ToggleFocus
//
// ⚠️ Left out of the list: cmd-shift-b -> outline_panel and ctrl-shift-g ->
// git_panel, which hold only while focus is OUTSIDE an editor. The
// JetBrains layer rebinds both in the `Editor` context (cmd-shift-b ->
// editor::GoToTypeDefinition, ctrl-shift-g -> editor::UndoSelection), and Zed
// resolves conflicts by context depth — an `Editor` binding beats a
// `Workspace` one (Zed's docs/src/key-bindings.md, "Precedence"). So while you
// are typing, those two keys are IDEA's navigation actions, not panel toggles.
// Use the panel toggles from the project panel / a non-editor focus, or rebind
// deliberately.
//
// So this file stays small on purpose — every binding below occupies a key
// verified free in BOTH the base macOS keymap and the JetBrains layer, and
// each earns its place. Rebinding anything above would fight IDEA muscle
// memory, which is the whole reason the JetBrains base was chosen.
[
  {
    "context": "Workspace",
    "bindings": {
      // lazygit in the center pane rather than the terminal dock, so the TUI
      // gets full height instead of a strip at the bottom.
      "alt-g": [
        "task::Spawn",
        { "task_name": "lazygit", "reveal_target": "center" }
      ]
    }
  },
  {
    "context": "Editor",
    "bindings": {
      // Long log lines and pasted output — wrap without touching settings.
      "alt-z": "editor::ToggleSoftWrap",
      // Inlay hints are on by default (JetBrains-style); this clears them
      // for a moment when reading dense code, without a settings round trip.
      "alt-i": "editor::ToggleInlayHints"
    }
  }
]
